## What does a successful check establish?

<img src="assets/figures/assurance-scope.png" alt="Formalization, checking, recording, returning and later deployment require different evidence." width="100%">

A solver result is conditional on the formal object, assumptions, checker, and checked obligation. A successful check alone does not establish that the formalization captures the intended task, that an explanation faithfully reports the result, or that later outputs of a solver-supervised model receive the same guarantee. [Read the framework](docs/taxonomy.md).

## Updates and contributions

**2026-10-12:** Initial public companion release: classified corpus, manuscript references, seven existing illustrations, and evaluation summaries. [Change log](CHANGELOG.md).

Suggestions for new papers, version updates, and metadata or classification corrections are welcome through [Issues](https://github.com/YishuaiGeng/Solvers-in-the-loop-Survey/issues/new/choose) or pull requests. Please include a public source and explain the relevant solver interaction. Suggestions are reviewed before entering a released corpus. See [contribution guidance](CONTRIBUTING.md) and the [maintenance policy](docs/maintenance.md).

